    "id": "AADC-00078_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This dataset is a record of the data in the ANARE Research Notes 78: Temperature-density, temperature-conductivity and conductivity-density relationships for marine-derived saline lake waters.  Authors: John A.E. Gibson, John M. Ferris and Harry R. Burton.\n\nAbstract per ANARE 78: Equations, determined using water samples from marine-derived saline lakes in Vestfold Hills, Antarctica, relating sigma T [=(density-1000) kg/m^3 at temperature between -15 degrees C and 40 degrees C to sigma 20, electrical conductivity at temperatures from -15 degrees C to 20 degrees C to conductivity at 0 degrees C, and sigma 20 to electrical conductivity at 0 degrees C are given.  These relationships allow in situ  sigma T to be calculated from in situ electrical conductivity and temperature data.\n\nFields in this data set are:\n\nSample Source (ie Lake Name and Depth)\nsigma 20 and quadratic coefficients\nTemperature\nComparison of sigma T using temperature-density relationships\nComparison of conductivities calculated",
